{"abstract":"Black-box optimization (BBO) problems arise in numerous scientic and engineering applications and are characterized by compu- tationally intensive objective functions, which severely limit the number of evaluations that can be performed. We present a robust set of features that analyze the tness landscape of BBO problems and show how an algorithm portfolio approach can exploit these general, problem indepen- dent features and outperform the utilization of any single minimization search strategy. We test our methodology on data from the GECCO Workshop on BBO Benchmarking 2012, which contains 21 state-of-the- art solvers run on 24 well-established functions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Tierney, Kevin","Malitsky, Yuri","Abell, Tinus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382545"],"event":{"end":"2013-01-11","place":"Catania, it","start":"2013-01-07","title":"Learning and Intelligent OptimizatioN Conference 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Algorithm portfolio","Black box optimization","Computationally intensive functions","Fitness landscape analysis","Optimization benchmarking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"features for exploiting black box optimization problem structure","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/76529050/bbo_lion7.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382545","identifier":[{"id":"84890946928","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-55bdbd21-074a-4023-a928-6a3feaf447c3"],"keyword":["Algorithm portfolio","Black-box optimization","Computationally intensive functions","Fitness landscape analysis","Optimization benchmarking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-80500E17C3EAA9E1788CB0E5F3D92870"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/76529050/bbo_lion7.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-44973-4_4","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kevin","key":"tierneypau","last":"Tierney","name":"Tierney, Kevin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuri","key":"malitskypau","last":"Malitsky","locid":"b7c1af22-ef9c-444e-a1d5-dfd1721d5a8d","name":"Malitsky, Yuri","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tinus","key":"abellpau","last":"Abell","name":"Abell, Tinus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-44973-4_4","isbn":["9783642449727"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"30-36","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Learning and Intelligent Optimization"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84890946928"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-55bdbd21-074a-4023-a928-6a3feaf447c3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Features for Exploiting Black-Box Optimization Problem Structure.","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382545","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
